      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-12-02_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>Dr. Williams' Pink Pills Effect Cures.</head>
        <p>Dr. Williams' Pink Pills Effect Cures.</p>
        <p>One of the busiest ladies in the west IN TOW-N. —• of London is Mrs. Phillips, who manages the fashionable boarding house at 13, Fopstone-road, Earl's Court. But at one time this lady was a great sufferer from sciatica and lumbago. "For years I had been subject to rheumatism," she saki," but two years ago I had an acute attack, with pains in my hip end hack. Sciatica extended from my hip to my heel, I also had a dull sickening pain in my back. I had decided to go into hospital, when a friend suggested that Dr. Williams' Pink Pills would cure me. With few doses I knew that they were effecting an improve- ment in my health. With one box the pains had left me. Soon I was able to get about,and when the second box was finished I was quite cured. Since that day I have never had ,sciatica, lumbago, or rheumatism." IN THE COUNTRY. Mr' George Davenport, 38, Portland-street, Collie Lanca- shire, Iris had a narrow escape from death by blood poisoning but Dr. IVilliains' Pink Pills restored him to perfect health and strength. He states :—" I contracted blood poisoning, and for four months I lay as if paralysed, with my nerves all shattered. I could neither sit nor stand. One day I read of Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, and sent for a box. They worked wonders, giving me appetite, strength. and new blood. A fort- night later I was a new man." ,Mrs. Davenport added : Nobody thought he would ever get better ; yet he is Ito-day in full health." A young woman at Bridge End, Comae, afflicted with St. Vitus dance was completely cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>• Thou i sands of men and woman n city and country praise Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, which have cured nzemia, indigestion, Eczema, Consumption, Kidney Disease, Bile, Rheumatism. Sciatica, St. Vitus' Dance, Nenvalgia, Paralysis, awl Locomotor Ataxy. A tonic and blood builder—not a purgative. Sold by all dealers; or sent direct, post tree, 2s. ad. for one box, or Els. 9d. for six, by Df. "^:ie Co., flolbarn-viadw- Lon&amp;</p>
        <p>COMMERCIAL FATLURES.—According to " Kemp's Mercantile Gazette," the total number of Commercial Failures recorded in England and Vales during the week ending Friday, :November 24th, was 190, viz. : New bankruptcy proceedings published in the London Gazette, 99; deeds of arrangement registered, 91. The respective numbers in the corresponding week of last year were: Bankruptcies, 83; deeds of arrangement us—total 151 ; being an increase of n 9. The total number of commercial failures recorded during the 47 weeks of the present year is 8,110 ; the total number recorded in the corresponding 47 weeks of last year was 8.056, showing nn increase of 84,</p>
