        <p>RUGBY UNION. STOCKTON FTEATK V. CIIESTER. COLLEGE.—PIayo d Chester on Saturday. Chester won the toss, Stock- ton Heath at once took on the attack, and Chester were forced to touch down. From the drop-out Chester paid a short visit to the Stockton fle:tth " 25." but Stockton Heath amain assumed the aggressive. Chester relieved by a punt, and Langley, receiving the ball, made a good run to the home quarters, where he transferred to K. ' Gibbs, who completed the run, and snored under the posts. H. Davenport converted. Chester now attacked, but good kicking by Jones relieved the pressure. From a scrum in the home half. Davenport secured, and beat- ing all opposition, kicked over the full back's head. Ferguson, who had followed up, was about to drop on the ball, when be was tackled. From tbe drop-out Chester at:sawed the aggressive, but were speedily repulsed. Even play followed till half-time came with the score: Stockton Heath. five points ;Chester College, nil. From the re-start Chester were Brien on the attack, and only the good play of 'Jones prevented a score. A touch-down relieved the pressure, but Cheater soon returuld to the attack, and taking every advantage of the slope took the game to</p>
